{{!--
  **A short list of strings, edited as a list.**  [BUILT 2026-11-13]

  Training, know-how and languages are `ArrayField`s and always have been. The editor was a single
  text input that the sheet joined on the way out and split on the way back, which made the
  separator part of the data: a comma inside a piece of know-how split it in two, and a training
  typed with a stray space became a different training from the one a tool bonus looks for.

  One partial rather than three copies, for the same reason the step editor is one: three copies
  is three places for the vocabulary to drift.

  `field` is the key under `system`, and the remove button carries an **index** rather than the
  text. That is the lesson the prune dialog paid for -- it matched an escaped name against a raw
  one and silently removed nothing -- and an index cannot be mangled on its way through HTML.
--}}
<div class="cr-entries__box">
<ul class="cr-entries">
  {{#each list}}
    <li class="cr-entry">
      <span class="cr-entry__text">{{this}}</span>
      <button type="button" class="cr-entry__x" data-action="removeEntry"
              data-field="{{../field}}" data-index="{{@index}}"
              data-tooltip="Remove {{this}}" aria-label="Remove {{this}}">&#10005;</button>
    </li>
  {{else}}
    <li class="cr-note cr-entries__none">Nothing yet.</li>
  {{/each}}
</ul>
<div class="cr-entries__add">
  <input type="text" class="cr-entry__new" data-field="{{field}}" placeholder="{{hint}}"
         aria-label="Add one" autocomplete="off">
  <button type="button" data-action="addEntry" data-field="{{field}}">Add</button>
</div>
</div>
